#X obj 702 8 xdac~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 286 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 An extended version of the standard [dac~] object that
accepts a list of output channels as its argument. In addition to single
channel numbers \, it also accepts range notation like 1:6 \, which
means "channels 1 through 6 inclusive". If no argument is given \,
channels 1 and 2 are used by default.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Multi-channel installations — connecting a patch
to a specific subset of audio outputs of a multi-channel sound card
(for example \, 1:6 for six speakers) \, without having to list every
channel number individually.;
#X text 250 279 • Channel remapping on the fly — using the @channels
property or the reverse \, rotate and shuffle methods to reorder the
outputs during a performance \, for example to swap left and right
or to rotate a surround layout.;
